                <pb facs="0838" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.54/1974a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-23T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>74. For your information. Repeat to Vladivostok.</p>
                <p>Although Davis and Abbott should already understand from previous instructions
                    that their duties are solely investigational, inform them upon their arrival
                    that Department does not desire this occasion to be used for the active
                    furtherance of business interests, nor should they be accompanied to Chita by
                    business men.</p>
                <p>Report full name, nationality and business of interpreter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
